2024-11-04T17:58:00 - Discarded instruction(didn't match expected format): "\nTo understand the instructions better, let’s improve the text of the document.\n\n# Meeting Scheduler Project\n\nThe **Meeting Scheduler Project** is a chatbot designed to assist users in scheduling meetings with ease and precision. It allows users to schedule meetings through natural language, and the chatbot's responses should be clear, concise, and informative.\n\nThe chatbot model must grasp the user's inputs and amass all the essential data required to arrange a meeting.\n\n## Necessary Data for Scheduling a Meeting:\n\n- **Participants**: (Names or emails of) the attendees who will be in attendance at the meeting.\n- **Date and Time**: The specific date and time when the meeting is scheduled to take place.\n- **Agenda**: (Purpose) of the meeting, i.e., the objectives and goals that the attendees aim to achieve during the meeting.\n- **Duration**: The length of time allocated for the meeting.\n\n### Handling Missing Data\n\nIf the user's input does not contain any of the necessary data, the chatbot should prompt the user to provide the missing information. The chatbot should specifically ask for:\n\n- **Participants**: If the participants are not mentioned, the model should request the names or emails of the attendees who will be present at the meeting.\n- **Date and Time**: If the date and time of the meeting are missing, the model should ask for the date and time when the meeting is scheduled to take place.\n- **Agenda**: If the agenda is not provided, the model should ask for the purpose of the meeting, i.e., the objectives and goals that the attendees aim to achieve during the meeting.\n- **Duration**: If the user does not mention the duration of the meeting, the model should prompt for a meeting duration.\n\n### Participant Clarification\n\nIf the user wants to schedule a meeting with an attendee and there are multiple attendees with the same name, the model should ask for the attendee's email to clarify the correct participant.\n\nHere are some examples of questions that you may ask in order to gather this information:\n* Question 1\nWhat is your goal for this meeting?\n* Question 2\nWho do you want to invite to the meeting?\n* Question 3\nWhen and where would you like to schedule this meeting?\n* Question 4\nHow long should this meeting last?\n* Question 5\nIs there any special information or document that we need to prepare for the meeting?"
